    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "9d9cb0048ad2a1598ce81efd73c1f643",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1688,
    "chunk_text": "It\u2019s the rule of law, stupid\n\nClose on the heels of the arrest of former President Ranil Wickremesinghe, Public Security Minister Ananda Wijepala thundered in Parliament that everyone was equal before the law. Whether the suspects were former Presidents or ex-IGPs did not matter any longer, he added. Anyone on the wrong side of the law would be prosecuted, he said. The CID arrested Wickremesinghe yesterday over alleged misuse of state funds for a private visit to the UK while he was the President. Produced before the Colombo Magistrate\u2019s Court, he was remanded last night. The matter is now before court, and it is best left to the learned judge concerned. Leader of the House and Minister Bimal Rathnayake said something similar amidst protests from the Opposition.\n\nIt was obvious that the government had been aware that the CID would arrest Wickremesinghe, and its members had come to Parliament to make statements and field questions thereon. Curiously, a pro-government YouTuber predicted Wickremesinghe\u2019s arrest a few days ago; he went so far as to say that he would close his YouTube channel if his prediction that Wickremesinghe would be arrested and remanded did not come true. Wickremesinghe\u2019s lawyers have lodged a complaint against the YouTuber with the CID.\n\nUnder every government, all are equal before the law except the bigwigs of the ruling party, just like the Pigs in Orwell\u2019s dystopian novella, Animal Farm. There have been few instances where some politicians were arrested while they were in power, but they are the exception that proves the rule, the prosecution of Minister Keheliya Rambukwella during the previous government being a case in point."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
