    "md5": "d2b84ccdea8d343b0ed2466be491988c",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1758,
    "chunk_text": "Under every government, all are equal before the law except the bigwigs of the ruling party, just like the Pigs in Orwell\u2019s dystopian novella, Animal Farm. There have been few instances where some politicians were arrested while they were in power, but they are the exception that proves the rule, the prosecution of Minister Keheliya Rambukwella during the previous government being a case in point.\n\nThe government is also defending Minister Kumar Jayakody despite a complaint against him that he caused a huge loss to the state coffers through tender irregularities during his stint at the Fertiliser Corporation. Any other politician with such an allegation against him would have been arrested by the CID. Minister Wasantha Samarasinghe and Deputy Minister Mahinda Jayasinghe are alleged to have leased out a property belonging to the National Workers\u2019 Institute using a forged deed.\n\nThey are lucky that they are members of the NPP government! Otherwise, they too would have been questioned by the CID and arrested. On 01 May, 2025, many buses transporting JVP/NPP supporters for their International Workers\u2019 Day rally in Colombo stopped in undesignated sections of the Southern Expressway in blatant violation of traffic laws. The government backers were seen having lunch and walking on the shoulder of the expressway while the police were looking on.\n\nAll of them should have been arrested and prosecuted. Disciplinary action should have been taken against former Speaker Asoka Ranwala for misleading Parliament by claiming to have a doctorate, and insisting that his claim was true even after stepping down as Speaker; he said he would produce proof of his PhD, but he has not done so yet. He should have been asked to resign from Parliament."
  },
