    "chunk_size_bytes": 982,
    "chunk_text": "Mr. Wickremesinghe assumed the presidency following the dramatic resignation of Gotabaya Rajapaksa in 2022, amid Sri Lanka\u2019s worst economic crisis in decades. His leadership is often credited with stabilising the nation\u2019s economy\u2014bringing down inflation, strengthening the rupee, and rebuilding foreign reserves.\n\nAgainst this backdrop, the arrest of a former president\u2014particularly one who played a pivotal role in safeguarding democratic institutions during times of upheaval\u2014raises serious questions. While allegations of financial misconduct must be investigated thoroughly, critics argue that detaining Mr. Wickremesinghe, even briefly, sets a troubling precedent.\n\nA more appropriate course, they contend, would have been to demand repayment of the disputed travel expenses rather than pursue punitive detention.\n\nThe unfolding case not only tests the government\u2019s commitment to justice but also risks deepening political divisions in an already fragile democracy."
