    "chunk_size_bytes": 1327,
    "chunk_text": "CBA grows into a technological leader in Sri Lanka backed by 55-year legacy\n\nCeylon Business Appliances (CBA) celebrates 55 years in Sri Lanka\u2019s technology sector, making a journey from humble beginnings to becoming an innovator in fintech, digital enterprise, and AI-powered solutions.\n\nFounded in 1970 by the late Charles Singhyar, CBA has weathered national challenges, including civil war, economic crises, and natural disasters, by prioritising a culture of integrity and employee loyalty.\n\n\u201cOur focus has never been just on numbers,\u201d said Sardha Fernando, Managing Director. \u201cIt\u2019s about standing by our values and our responsibility to society. That defines our growth.\u201d\n\nThe company has evolved from servicing banks to pioneering national firsts, including cashless vending solutions, payment systems for over 60,000 merchants, virtual card platforms, and e-ticketing for public transport. Recently, CBA has expanded into EduTech, HealthTech, and is now driving AI technologies to uplift operational efficiencies across industries.\n\nTata Motors and DIMO strengthen partnership with major vehicle launch in Sri Lanka\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
