    "chunk_text": "However, the fiscal and external sectors showed some contrasting trends. The value of Treasury Bills and Bonds held by foreign investors decreased by 1%, a sign that some foreign investors are pulling back from Sri Lankan government securities. Despite this, the recent T-Bill auction was oversubscribed by two times, indicating strong local demand.\n\nGlobal oil prices were volatile and ended the week higher. Brent and WTI crude oil prices saw increases of $1.69 and $0.54 per barrel, respectively. This was influenced by a larger-than-expected drop in US crude oil inventories and uncertainty surrounding a potential peace deal between the US, Russia, and Ukraine. Higher global oil prices could impact Sri Lanka\u2019s import costs in the future.\n\nAll eyes will be on the National Consumer Price Index for August to see if this inflationary trend gains momentum.\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
