    "chunk_text": "He has represented Sri Lanka internationally at forums such as the United Nations World Tourism Organisation (UNWTO), South Asian Association for Regional Cooperation (SAARC), Pacific Asia Travel Association (PATA), and Bay of Bengal Initiative for Multi-Sectoral Technical and Economic Cooperation (BIMSTEC), actively strengthening the country\u2019s global partnerships and securing multilateral support for the tourism sector.\n\nInternationally, he was awarded a United Nations Institute for Training and Research (UNITAR) Fellowship in International Affairs Management at the United Nations Headquarters, undertook a UNWTO Practicum on global tourism administration, and was recognised at George Washington University, USA, as a Visiting Research Fellow in Tourism. In addition, he is the Founder and Owner of South Asia Multidisciplinary Advisory Services (SAMAS).\n\nThe award reflects not only his personal dedication but also the broader impact of his work in shaping sustainable policies, community-based tourism initiatives, and international collaborations that continue to benefit the nation\u2019s economy and cultural identity."
