    "chunk_size_bytes": 1755,
    "chunk_text": "38th Annual Conference and 4th National  Apex Awards of  the OPA honours excellence, fosters professional collaboration\n\nThe Organisation of Professional Associations of Sri Lanka (OPA) successfully hosted its 38th Annual Conference and the prestigious 4th National Apex Awards on 19 and 20 August, at the Cinnamon Life, Colombo. The event commenced with a distinguished inaugural ceremony, graced by the Chief Guest \u2013 Speaker of the Parliament of Sri Lanka Dr. Jagath Wickramaratne, and attended by leading figures from the professional sector.\n\nIn his welcome address, OPA President Sujeewa Lal Dahanayake, reaffirmed the OPA\u2019s commitment to national development through professional collaboration and active engagement with the Government. He emphasised the significance of the Annual Conference, which was taking place during the 50th anniversary of the OPA, marking five decades of multidisciplinary professional unity and collective efforts toward the advancement of the nation.\n\nThis was followed by a speech by President-Elect and Annual Conference Committee Chairman Jayantha Gallehewa who elaborated on the relevance and timeliness of the conference theme, \u201cResilience and Outpace Redefined: Thriving and Adapting.\u201d He stressed the crucial need for resilience and adaptability to drive Sri Lanka\u2019s progress, particularly at this pivotal juncture in its development journey.\n\nIn his address, the Chief Guest Dr. Jagath Wickramaratne, highlighted the vital role of professionals in nation-building, fostering innovation, and contributing to a knowledge-based economy.\n\nSpeaker of the Parliament of Sri Lanka Dr. Jagath Wickramaratne\n\nTreasury and Ministry of Finance Planning and Economic Development Secretary Dr. Harshana Suriyapperuma"
