    "md5": "0f2fe70c3864f220edd1df8244b9c4f2",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1893,
    "chunk_text": "An evening of music, unity and gratitude\n\nThe local scene is inundated with musical events, with happenings here, there, and everywhere!\n\nYes, music fans have a choice, but not much variety to choose from as, practically, the same artistes are featured at most venues.\n\nHowever, it\u2019s going to be an entirely different scene when the spotlight falls on the Cinnamon Lakeside A/C Marquee, on Saturday, 13th September, where glamour, music, and gratitude will merge into one unforgettable evening at The Gajaba Unity Fest 2025.\n\nAccording to the media coordinator of the 2025 event, Maneka Liyanage, The Gajaba Unity Fest is held annually and is organised by the Gajaba Veterans Association, to promote unity, entertainment, and welfare of the Gajaba Regiment veterans and their families.\n\nShe went on to say that the festival aims to raise funds for the welfare of Gajaba Regiment veterans, their families, and the families of war heroes who were disabled or killed in action.\n\nOrganised by Rideem Entertainment, together with the Gajaba Veterans Association, this concert is more than a celebration of music, says Maneka.\n\nDescribing the setup for the evening of Saturday, 13th September, she said:\n\n\u201cIt\u2019s a heartfelt tribute to the bravery and sacrifice of Sri Lanka\u2019s disabled soldiers and their families, and we have got the lineup to do the needful on 13th September.\n\n\u201cIn the spotlight will be Sohan Weerasinghe , the legendary singer/entertainer, with an irresistible stage presence; Mariazelle Goonetilleke, whose songs remain timeless; Lahiru Perera, the ultimate crowd-mover, bringing unstoppable energy; and Kavindi Kulasena, the new-age sensation with a voice that commands attention; and with Dominic Kellar as compere.\n\n\u201cBacking the singers will be the electrifying Redeemers Band, guaranteeing a performance that will keep hearts racing and feet moving all night long."
