    "md5": "5dd21f43e3c02ca0d0ff7206fcf5b34c",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1941,
    "chunk_text": "Ranil gets bail\n\nFormer President Ranil Wickremesinghe, arrested and remanded on Friday (22) for alleged misuse of state funds during a visit to London, while in office, was granted bail yesterday.\n\nLarge crowds flocked to Colombo yesterday, when the Colombo Fort Magistrate\u2019s Court took up the case against Wickremesinghe. In a rare show of unity, the Opposition parties have circled the wagons around Wickremesinghe, vowing to defeat what they describe as a witch-hunt against the political rivals of the government. They have accused the JVP, which leads the ruling NPP coalition, of striving to create a one-party rule.\n\nThe warring political leaders have said they hold the judiciary in high esteem, and their protests are against the NPP government and the CID, which, they say, is all out to silence democratic dissent at the behest of its political masters. Among those who have rallied around Wickremesinghe are some of his sworn political enemies. They have rightly condemned the politicisation of the police and selective enforcement, but one cannot endorse the timing of yesterday\u2019s protest. The deplorable practice of political parties and other organisations holding demonstrations while cases pertaining to issues that affect their interests are being heard, should be discontinued, for such events, silent or otherwise, are tantamount to efforts to influence, if not intimidate, the judiciary.\n\nThe government has sought to lump all those who are defending Wickremesinghe together and vilify them as rogues. We can see some undesirables among the defenders of the former President. Even Mervyn Silva has taken up the cudgels for Wickremesinghe\u2019s rights! However, the government will be mistaken if it thinks it can hoodwink the public with the help of a false dichotomy. Every political party has its share of rogues. The government has unwittingly provided the Opposition, which was in disarray, with a rallying point."
  },
