    "chunk_size_bytes": 1351,
    "chunk_text": "The government has sought to lump all those who are defending Wickremesinghe together and vilify them as rogues. We can see some undesirables among the defenders of the former President. Even Mervyn Silva has taken up the cudgels for Wickremesinghe\u2019s rights! However, the government will be mistaken if it thinks it can hoodwink the public with the help of a false dichotomy. Every political party has its share of rogues. The government has unwittingly provided the Opposition, which was in disarray, with a rallying point.\n\nThe UNP, which is playing the victim card today, ruined Sri Lankan politics; it did everything in its power to destroy the multiparty system and establish a one-party rule from 1977 to 1994. Thankfully, its efforts failed but they plunged the country into a bloodbath, with the JVP launching its second uprising. Attacks on the Opposition continued under the SLFP-led People\u2019s Alliance government, and they took a turn for the worse under the UPFA government under Mahinda Rajapaksa\u2019s presidency. President Rajapaksa debilitated all other political parties by causing splits in them and engineering mass crossovers. Wickremesinghe himself stands accused of having broken up political parties. The UNP-led Yahapalana government used the CID to do its dirty work with the blessing of Wickremesinghe as the Prime Minister."
