    "chunk_text": "The UNP, which is playing the victim card today, ruined Sri Lankan politics; it did everything in its power to destroy the multiparty system and establish a one-party rule from 1977 to 1994. Thankfully, its efforts failed but they plunged the country into a bloodbath, with the JVP launching its second uprising. Attacks on the Opposition continued under the SLFP-led People\u2019s Alliance government, and they took a turn for the worse under the UPFA government under Mahinda Rajapaksa\u2019s presidency. President Rajapaksa debilitated all other political parties by causing splits in them and engineering mass crossovers. Wickremesinghe himself stands accused of having broken up political parties. The UNP-led Yahapalana government used the CID to do its dirty work with the blessing of Wickremesinghe as the Prime Minister.\n\nIt is the fervent hope of every right-thinking citizen that all those who are responsible for corrupt practices and abuse of power will be brought to justice. But that should be done in a proper manner and not according to any political agenda. In the case of Wickremesinghe, the CID has not properly investigated allegations against him; obviously, it was in a mighty hurry to arrest him to please the government. Politically motivated arrests are counterproductive as has been the experience of all past governments that resorted to them out of desperation.\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
