    "chunk_size_bytes": 1473,
    "chunk_text": "From farm to future: Cargills nurtures Sri Lanka\u2019s next generation\n\nCargills (Ceylon) PLC presented educational scholarships to students from farming communities at a ceremony held on 29th August 2025, an initiative which is part of Cargills\u2019 Sarubima programme.\n\nThe event was graced by K. D. Lal Kantha, Minister of Agriculture, Livestock, Land, and Irrigation, as the Chief Guest, and was attended by D. P. Wickramasinghe, Secretary to the Ministry and distinguished invitees from international development organizations, and directors and senior management of Cargills.\n\nThis year, the company allocated over Rs. 115 million through the Cargills Sarubima programme to support both student scholarships and rural community projects. Of this, over Rs. 50 million is dedicated to educational scholarships, benefiting over 1,300 students through Grade 5 and A/Level scholarships, vocational training, and laptops for university students. Over Rs. 60 million is allocated to community development initiatives, including upgraded libraries, smart classrooms, clean water systems, sanitation facilities and preschool infrastructure enhancements.\n\nA section of the scholarship recipients poses for a group photograph at the ceremony\n\nBeyond providing scholarships and developing community infrastructure, the Cargills Sarubima programme aims to enhance students\u2019 knowledge by improving access to quality education and equipping them to become future leaders of Sri Lanka."
