    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka coconut prices rise 7.4-pct, more nuts offered\n\nECONOMYNEXT \u2013 Sri Lanka\u2019s average coconut prices climbed 7.4 percent to a three week high at a weekly auction, Coconut Development Authority data showed.\n\nThe average price for 1,000 nuts was 144,000.12 rupees on August 28.\n\nThe number of nuts offered rose to 639,098 from 551,525 a week earlier, while nuts sold climbed to 531,960 from 519,803.\n\n\u201cThe highest or the lowest price for a nut was not declared,\u201d CDA officials told EconomyNext.\n\nThe Coconut Development Authority has not declared the highest and the lowest price for a nut since July 4.\n\nSri Lanka\u2019s coconut production had recovered strongly in the second quarter of 2025.\n\nJune production has climbed 18 percent to 289.5 million nuts from a year earlier, official data showed.\n\nSri Lanka coconut recovers strongly June 2025, topping last year\u2019s level\n\nIn the local market, the wholesale price for a large nut was 170-180 rupees, while small nuts were 150-160 a piece on August 28.\n\nLocal wholesale prices of coconut oil were 840,000 to 880,000 rupees per metric ton. (Colombo/Sep1/2025)"
