    "chunk_text": "CSE sets up yet another record as ASPI hits 21,000 index points\n\nThe CSE set up another record yesterday when the All Share Price Index surpassed 21,000 Index points, market analysts said.\n\nThe reason for the high-point in trading was the low interest regime coupled with conducive economic policies which enabled the market to grow, analysts explained.\n\nAmid those developments indices gave out mixed signals. The All Share Price Index went up by 52.3 points while the S and P SL20 declined by 4.07 points.\n\nTurnover stood at Rs 13.2 billion with eleven crossings. The main crossings were reported in JKH, which crossed 331 million shares to the tune of Rs 5.38 billion; its shares traded at Rs 23, Commercial Bank 7.1 million shares crossed to the tune of Rs 1.4 billion; its shares traded at Rs 193, CT Holdings 500,000 shares crossed for Rs 351 million; its shares sold at Rs 702, Dialog Axiata 3.6 million shares crossed to the tune of Rs 95 million; its shares traded at Rs 93, VallibelOne one million shares crossed to the tune of Rs 93 million; its shares traded at Rs 93.\n\nAsian Hotel Properties one million shares crossed to the tune of Rs 70 million; its shares traded at Rs 70, Hemas Holdings 2.1 million shares crossed for Rs 64 million and its shares sold at Rs 30.50, Lanka IOC 300,000 shares crossed to the tune of Rs 40.5 million; its shares traded at Rs 135, Haylays 175,000 shares crossed for Rs 30.6 million; its shares fetched Rs 135."
