    "chunk_size_bytes": 1125,
    "chunk_text": "The travel bug has not spared the members of the incumbent administration either despite their much-avowed commitment to austerity measures. They travel long distances to attend various ceremonies. President Anura Kumara Dissanayake was in the North yesterday to commence some development projects there. Northern development, no doubt, must figure high on the government\u2019s agenda, but should the President, ministers and state officials go all the way from Colombo to attend such events, for the public has to bear the cost of their travel, etc. Security arrangements alone cost the public an arm and a leg.\n\nOne may recall that President Dissanayake and Indian Prime Minister Narendra Modi launched the Sampur solar energy project via a virtual platform in April. This is the best way for the government leaders and state officials to attend ceremonies. They should remain mindful of the country\u2019s economic problems and do everything possible to save state funds. Having obtained a popular mandate to bring about a major system overhaul, the NPP politicians are duty-bound to set examples and precedents, aren\u2019t they?"
