    "chunk_text": "One may recall that President Dissanayake and Indian Prime Minister Narendra Modi launched the Sampur solar energy project via a virtual platform in April. This is the best way for the government leaders and state officials to attend ceremonies. They should remain mindful of the country\u2019s economic problems and do everything possible to save state funds. Having obtained a popular mandate to bring about a major system overhaul, the NPP politicians are duty-bound to set examples and precedents, aren\u2019t they?\n\nWanderlust seems to be a shared characteristic of all Sri Lankan political leaders. We once said in an editorial comment that President Sirisena was travelling overseas at such a rate that while going out, he might meet himself coming in, at the BIA. A wag asks whether President Dissanayake is determined to break that record.\n\nIt is hoped that politicians and officials will rest their legs and tongues and set their minds to what needs to be done to revitalise the economy and improve the people\u2019s lot.\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
