    "md5": "4f4565a09935aee1411b5b08a8b61a99",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1820,
    "chunk_text": "Mob justice?\n\nA Frontline Socialist Party (FSP) office in Yakkala came under attack yesterday morning; four persons suffered injuries. The FSP, an offshoot of the JVP, blamed a group of JVP politicians for the attack, demanding that the police arrest them forthwith. The FSP activists said the attackers were forcibly occupying their office, and named the JVP politicians who had allegedly led the attack. But the police ignored their call.\n\nWhat one gathers from a video footage of yesterday\u2019s incident is that the manner in which the police handled the situation smacked of their partiality towards the government members, as the FSP has claimed. IGP Priyantha Weerasooriya keeps saying there is no political interference in the police at present, and they can act independently and impartially. But instead of taking action against the alleged attackers, the police yesterday asked the protesting FSP members to leave, make complaints and take the issue to court. There is reason to believe that they would have acted differently if the FSP activists had been responsible for the attack.\n\nYesterday\u2019s incident at Yakkala is proof that the police have not mended their ways; it reminds us of how they baulked at taking action against a group of pro-government goons who set upon the Aragalaya protesters at Galle Face in 2022. If they had used force against the SLPP goons, stopping them from entering the protest site, attacks on the peaceful protesters and the subsequent spree of retaliatory violence could have been prevented. The then IGP Deshabandu Tennakoon is facing legal action against his failure to prevent the savage attacks led by SLPP politicians. Gotabaya Rajapaksa, who was the President at the time, is to be summoned by the CID to record a statement on those attacks, according to media reports."
  },
