    "chunk_size_bytes": 1848,
    "chunk_text": "Yesterday\u2019s incident at Yakkala is proof that the police have not mended their ways; it reminds us of how they baulked at taking action against a group of pro-government goons who set upon the Aragalaya protesters at Galle Face in 2022. If they had used force against the SLPP goons, stopping them from entering the protest site, attacks on the peaceful protesters and the subsequent spree of retaliatory violence could have been prevented. The then IGP Deshabandu Tennakoon is facing legal action against his failure to prevent the savage attacks led by SLPP politicians. Gotabaya Rajapaksa, who was the President at the time, is to be summoned by the CID to record a statement on those attacks, according to media reports.\n\nThe FSP says it has occupied the building where its Yakkala office is located for about 13 years, and therefore it has a right to be there. However, the JVP members involved in yesterday\u2019s incident produced what they described as the judgement in a case they had filed against the FSP over the disputed office; they said the court had ruled in their favour, and therefore the building was rightfully theirs. If so, the judicial decision should be carried out by an officer authorised by the judiciary to do so and not by the JVP cadres led by their organisers and MPs. If the winning side in a court case is allowed to implement judicial decisions according to their whims and fancies, how can the government claim that the rule of law has been restored and everyone is equal before the law?\n\nFormer Deputy Minister Nimal Lanza has been arrested and remanded over an incident where he allegedly assaulted a person about 20 years ago; he should have been arrested much earlier. So, there is no reason why the police should not arrest those who stormed and seized the FSP office, injuring four persons including a woman."
