    "md5": "90ec3aeadcef405a5a1a4fded94d2af1",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1921,
    "chunk_text": "Dr Rohantha Athukorala appointed to Lotus Hydro Power Board\n\nBusiness professional Dr Rohantha Athukorala with a 23 years British Multinational experience of UNILEVER, ReckittBenckiser and United Nations( UNOPS) has been appointed to the Board of Lotus Hydro Power PLC \u2013 a leading renewable energy in Sri Lanka. Headquartered in Colombo, Sri Lanka, the company is a prominent corporation specializing in the development and operation of renewable energy sources. The company currently oversees the operation of four active power plants strategically located in the Rathnapura, Kandy, and Nuwara Eliya regions. The company is a proponent for supplying green energy while safeguarding the environment. I am excited to serve an organization that has so far generated over 65,000 tons of Carbon Credits and 15.4 Gwh of Green Energy in Sri Lanka said Athukorala.\n\nAn advocate for driving \u201d Ethically manufactured proposition\u201d for Sri Lanka globally, when Dr Athukorala was the Chairman Sri Lanka Export Development Board and Sri Lanka Tourism is currently is the Vice Chairman of the World Tourism Council with its head quarters in Luncun, China.\n\nAn expert on brand marketing trained by top multinationals such as Unilever, Reckitt Benckiser, and DiverseyLever India. His 23 year extensive career includes serving as the Country Head for Sri Lanka and the Maldives, where he has made significant contributions to brand development and business development at national level. His achievements have been recognized with multiple accolades, including the prestigious \u2018Marketing Achiever\u2019 award from the Chartered Institute of Marketing and the Business Achiever award from the Postgraduate Institute of Management (PIM) at the University of Sri Jayewardenepura and Abdul Kalam Service to the nation award. He is the only Sri Lankan to be awarded the \u201d Rotary People of Action\u201d global award by Rotary International."
