    "language": "en",
    "md5": "5cec22f9529301230573bd7d8ee43c68",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1727,
    "chunk_text": "Instead of ushering in a durable peace as expected, the Indo-Lanka Accord paved the way for more violence and bloodshed. The Liberation Tigers of Tamil Eelam (LTTE) led by its supremo Veluppillai Prabhakaran refused to accept the accord and went back to war. Soon a full-fledged guerrilla war was waged by the LTTE against the IPKF in the North and East.\n\nThe second JVP insurgency lasting for more than three years resulted in thousands of people being brutally killed by both the JVP as well as the counter insurgency forces comprising Police, paramilitary and security personnel. Tens of thousands of Sinhala youth were massacred by agents of the State.  Thousands were incarcerated. Hundreds went underground.Rohana Wijeweera, his deputy Upatissa Gamanayake along with 14 of the 15 member JVP Politburo were killed. The only JVP Politburo member to survive was  Somawansa Amerasinghe.He escaped to India and from there went to Europe.\n\nMost of the JVP top leaders today including  Anura Kumara Dissanayake, ministers Bimal Rathnayake, Vijitha Herath and secretary Tilvin Silva were members of the JVP during this second JVP insurgency period. They underwent much suffering and witnessed the violence unleashed against their comrades. To this second generation JVP stalwarts the first insurgency during Mrs.Bandaranaike\u2019s reign was only a distant memory. To them the reality was the bitter experience they underwent during UNP rule.They hate that UNP Govt with a passionate vengeance.\n\nRanil Wickremesinghe  is the last cabinet minister from those UNP Governments who is  active in politics today. Besides he has been leading the UNP for the last 30 years. Ranil in that sense represents and symbolises the UNP to the JVP."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
    "doc_id": "2025-09-05-dbsjeyarajcom-419a7ad1",
    "num": "dbsjeyarajcom-419a7ad1",
    "date_str": "2025-09-05",
    "description": "Has the JVP led NPP Launched a Political Witch Hunt Targeting  Former  President Ranil Wickremesinghe ?",
