    "chunk_size_bytes": 520,
    "chunk_text": "After Move Forward was blocked from taking power, Pheu Thai had one of its candidates, real estate executive Srettha Thavisin, approved as prime minister to lead a coalition government. But he served just a year before the Constitutional Court dismissed him from office for ethical violations.\n\nSrettha\u2019s replacement Paetongtarn, former Prime Minister Thaksin Shinawatra\u2019s daughter, also lasted just a year in office.\n\nIts withdrawal left Pheu Thai\u2019s coalition with just a tiny and unstable majority in Parliament."
